1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,070
Gus is trying to open a

2
00:00:01,080 --> 00:00:03,140
plane door seven miles up, and

3
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:04,660
he's in no danger at all.

4
00:00:04,704 --> 00:00:06,424
It's three in the afternoon, he

5
00:00:06,434 --> 00:00:07,734
just woke up from a nap,

6
00:00:07,914 --> 00:00:09,274
and he thinks it's the bathroom.

7
00:00:09,328 --> 00:00:10,388
His wife screams.

8
00:00:10,598 --> 00:00:12,208
His neighbor grabs his seat belt.

9
00:00:12,262 --> 00:00:13,312
Gus pulls harder.

10
00:00:13,382 --> 00:00:13,932
Nothing.

11
00:00:14,112 --> 00:00:14,862
He puts a foot on the

12
00:00:14,872 --> 00:00:15,282
wall.

13
00:00:15,292 --> 00:00:16,042
Still nothing.

14
00:00:16,096 --> 00:00:16,706
But wait.

15
00:00:16,716 --> 00:00:17,916
Gus isn't that weak.

16
00:00:18,086 --> 00:00:19,486
So what's holding the door shut?

17
00:00:19,530 --> 00:00:20,760
You see, up here the air

18
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:21,850
outside is thin.

19
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:23,560
It presses a fifth as hard

20
00:00:23,570 --> 00:00:24,790
as the air on the ground.

21
00:00:24,834 --> 00:00:25,964
So the cabin is pumped up

22
00:00:25,974 --> 00:00:27,464
like a tire, and all that

23
00:00:27,474 --> 00:00:28,304
air wants out.

24
00:00:28,348 --> 00:00:29,858
It leans on every square inch

25
00:00:29,868 --> 00:00:31,768
of the door, eight pounds harder

26
00:00:31,778 --> 00:00:33,458
than the thin air outside pushes

27
00:00:33,468 --> 00:00:33,758
back.

28
00:00:33,812 --> 00:00:34,712
And a door has a lot

29
00:00:34,722 --> 00:00:35,732
of square inches.

30
00:00:35,992 --> 00:00:37,192
Add them up, and you get

31
00:00:37,202 --> 00:00:38,882
almost twenty thousand pounds.

32
00:00:38,936 --> 00:00:39,846
That is the weight of four

33
00:00:39,856 --> 00:00:41,516
cars, parked on the door.

34
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:42,770
Ever pull a suction cup off

35
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:43,400
a window?

36
00:00:43,610 --> 00:00:44,550
There's no glue.

37
00:00:44,710 --> 00:00:46,100
It's just air pushing on one

38
00:00:46,110 --> 00:00:46,570
side.

39
00:00:46,624 --> 00:00:48,144
A plane door is a plug,

40
00:00:48,354 --> 00:00:49,664
a bit bigger than its hole,

41
00:00:49,674 --> 00:00:50,664
so it has to come in

42
00:00:50,674 --> 00:00:51,664
before it swings out.

43
00:00:51,708 --> 00:00:53,048
To open it, Gus would have

44
00:00:53,058 --> 00:00:54,758
to drag in all four cars.

45
00:00:54,812 --> 00:00:56,392
Luckily, nobody can do that.

46
00:00:56,436 --> 00:00:57,886
Unluckily, he still needs the

47
00:00:57,896 --> 00:00:59,906
bathroom, and the door only lets

48
00:00:59,916 --> 00:01:00,916
go on the ground.

49
00:01:00,970 --> 00:01:02,360
So he tries the next door,

50
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:03,710
the one door on this plane

51
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:04,390
he can open.

52
00:01:04,444 --> 00:01:05,464
It's taken.
